---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import AdSlot from '@components/AdSlot.astro';
---

<Layout
  lang="en"
  title="Palworld 1.0 Complete Guide - New Areas, 9 Tower Bosses, Mutation & Awakening"
  description="Full Palworld 1.0 guide. The 2026-07-10 launch: level cap 65 to 80, Sunreach, the World Tree, all 9 tower bosses, Mutation and Awakening, 44 new accessories, and the latest patch v1.0.5."
>
  <article class="guide-content">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/en/guides/">Guides</a> › Palworld 1.0</p>
      <h1>🆕 Palworld 1.0 Complete Guide: New Areas, 9 Tower Bosses, Mutation & Awakening</h1>
      <p class="text-secondary">
        Released 2026-07-10 (patch 1.100.427) · Out of Early Access · Level cap 65 → 80 · Latest version v1.0.5
      </p>
    </header>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>What 1.0 Actually Changed</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Level cap 65 → 80</strong>: every tower boss gains a "Hard" difficulty, all of them sitting between Lv 72 and Lv 80</li>
        <li><strong>72 new Pals</strong> (47 new species + 25 variants), bringing the Paldex to <strong>287</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Two new regions</strong>: the floating sky islands of <strong>Sunreach</strong> (Lv 60-70) and <strong>The World Tree</strong> (Lv 70-80)</li>
        <li><strong>9 tower bosses</strong>: the original 5 plus Feybreak, Moonflower, Azure Covenant and the World Tree</li>
        <li><strong>Mutation</strong> and <strong>Awakening</strong>, two brand-new progression systems</li>
        <li><strong>44 new accessories</strong>, Ancient Series armour, and PvP</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Level Cap 80: Your Old Gear Is Outdated</h2>
      <p>
        1.0 raises the player level cap from <strong>65 to 80</strong>. That number change
        rewrites two things:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>The "Hard" tower boss difficulty</strong>: 8 of the 9 towers now have a Hard
          version between Lv 72 and Lv 80, with 5-10x the HP of the Normal version.
          Full data in the <a href="/en/guides/boss-guide/">boss guide</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ancient Series armour</strong>: the new Ancient gear is the answer at level 80,
          while the <a href="/en/tech-tree/Battle_Armor_Grade_04_Steal_Cold/">Pal Metal Armor</a>
          set loses most of its value past level 70.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        To actually push past level 80 you need <strong>Awakening</strong> - a system that uses
        <strong>Radiant Gems</strong> from the World Tree to unlock extra levels for a Pal.
        The Awakening section below covers the details.
      </p>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>New Region 1: Sunreach (Lv 60-70)</h2>
      <p>
        Sunreach is a <strong>floating archipelago of sky islands</strong> and the mid-to-late
        story area of 1.0. Enemy levels sit between <strong>60 and 70</strong>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Soralite ore</strong> - mined from the <a href="/en/tech-tree/SkyIslandOrePit/">Soralite Quarry</a>, the base material for 1.0 endgame gear</li>
        <li><strong>Azure Covenant Tower</strong> - the tower in this region, guarded by <strong>Auri &amp; Shaolong</strong> at <strong>Lv 68</strong> on Normal with 327,600 HP</li>
        <li><strong>Azure Covenant Flag Set</strong> (unlocks at Lv 71) is the matching base decoration</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The sky weapons unlock in the same stretch - Mechanical Bow, Combat SMG, Prototype Shotgun
        and Heavy Assault Rifle all arrive between Lv 66 and Lv 70, and they are the main power
        spike before tower 8.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>New Region 2: The World Tree (Lv 70-80)</h2>
      <p>
        The World Tree is the <strong>final region of 1.0</strong> and the arena of the final
        tower boss Zenara &amp; Astralym. Enemy levels run <strong>70 to 80</strong>, making it
        a clean continuation of the Sunreach level curve.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Paloxite</strong> - the World Tree's own ore, unlocked as <a href="/en/tech-tree/WorldTreeIngot/">WorldTreeIngot</a> at Lv 74</li>
        <li><strong>Radiant Gems</strong> - the core material of the Awakening system</li>
        <li><strong>Ancient Civilization Relic</strong> - the material behind the Ancient Series equipment</li>
        <li><strong>World Tree passive skills</strong> - a batch of passives <strong>above the usual Rainbow tier</strong>, including one that trades +50% Attack for reduced Defense</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The World Tree also unlocks the endgame tech line: the
        <a href="/en/tech-tree/AncientRelicRecycler/">Ancient Relic Recycler</a>,
        <a href="/en/tech-tree/PalSphere_Ancient_2/">Ancient Sphere</a> and the rest of the
        Ancient Series.
      </p>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>7 New Small Islands</h2>
      <p>
        1.0 also adds <strong>7 new islands</strong> built around volcano, desert and ruins
        themes. Unlike the two story regions these are open-world sandbox spots, good for
        farming materials and catching low-level Pals.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Loess Plains</strong>, <strong>Scorched Ashland</strong>, <strong>Withered Seaside</strong>, <strong>Emberstone Plateau</strong> - volcano and ashland themes</li>
        <li><strong>Frozen Coral Hill</strong>, <strong>Sunlit Isle</strong>, <strong>Oasis Isle</strong>, <strong>Isle of the Glacial Core</strong> - ice and islet themes</li>
        <li><strong>Fortress Ruins</strong>, <strong>Golden Hills</strong>, <strong>Autumn Rocks</strong> - ruins themes</li>
        <li>Smaller islets such as Flamepulse Islet, Islet of Circular Ruins, Scouring Islet, Bicornis Islet, Glacial Memento Islet, Sandstone Gate Islet and Suncrest Islet</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Every region and its level range is catalogued in the
        <a href="/en/regions/">Palworld region index</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>The 9 Tower Bosses: Normal and Hard</h2>
      <p>
        After 1.0 there are <strong>9 towers</strong>, and every tower boss has both a Normal and
        a Hard difficulty. The first five are the original Palpagos towers; the other four are
        Feybreak, Moonflower, Azure Covenant in Sunreach, and the final World Tree tower.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Rayne Syndicate Tower</strong> — Zoe &amp; Grizzbolt (Electric) | Normal Lv 10 / HP 12,900 | Hard Lv 72 / HP 464,000</li>
        <li><strong>Free Pal Alliance Tower</strong> — Lily &amp; Lyleen (Grass) | Normal Lv 20 / HP 42,500 | Hard Lv 74 / HP 494,000</li>
        <li><strong>Brothers of the Eternal Pyre Tower</strong> — Axel &amp; Orserk (Dragon, Electric) | Normal Lv 30 / HP 53,750 | Hard Lv 76 / HP 514,800</li>
        <li><strong>PIDF Tower</strong> — Marcus &amp; Faleris (Fire) | Normal Lv 40 / HP 72,900 | Hard Lv 78 / HP 526,900</li>
        <li><strong>PAL Genetic Research Unit Tower</strong> — Victor &amp; Shadowbeak (Dark) | Normal Lv 50 / HP 105,000 | Hard Lv 80 / HP 570,000</li>
        <li><strong>Moonflower Tower</strong> — Saya &amp; Selyne (Dark, Neutral) | Normal Lv 55 / HP 234,900 | Hard Lv 80 / HP 567,300</li>
        <li><strong>Feybreak Tower</strong> — Bjorn &amp; Bastigor (Ice) | Normal Lv 60 / HP 310,000 | Hard Lv 80 / HP 487,500</li>
        <li><strong>Azure Covenant Tower</strong> — Auri &amp; Shaolong (Dragon, Water) | Normal Lv 68 / HP 327,600 | Hard Lv 80 / HP 501,600</li>
        <li><strong>Final tower</strong> — Zenara &amp; Astralym | Lv 80 / HP 420,000 (no Hard version)</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Normal difficulty is the main-story path; <strong>Hard is a uniform Lv 72-80 endgame
        gauntlet</strong> with HP pools approaching 600,000. Team composition and positioning
        details are in the <a href="/en/guides/boss-guide/">full boss guide</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Mutation: Breeding Better Eggs</h2>
      <p>
        1.0 adds <strong>Mutation</strong> to the breeding system. Mutated eggs have
        <strong>higher base stats</strong> and carry a <strong>unique passive skill</strong> -
        something normal breeding simply cannot produce.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Mutant eggs roll better base stats and level up faster</li>
        <li>They come with an exclusive passive, so you lock in a trait at the egg stage</li>
        <li>Stacking Mutation with Awakening is the intended way to build a 1.0 core team</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To work out exact recipes, use our <a href="/en/breeding/">breeding calculator</a>:
        it is built on 40,972 breeding edges covering every valid pairing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Awakening: Breaking the Cap with Radiant Gems</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Awakening</strong> is 1.0's long-term growth system. Using
        <strong>Radiant Gems</strong> from the World Tree, you can unlock levels for a Pal
        beyond the standard cap.
      </p>
      <p>
        The practical effect: <strong>level 80 is not the ceiling</strong>. Beating Zenara &amp;
        Astralym needs more than a flat level 80 in Ancient gear - your core Pals need to be
        awakened further. That is why Radiant Gems are one of the scarcest resources in 1.0.
      </p>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Gear: 44 New Accessories and Ancient Series Armour</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>44 new accessories</strong>: 1.0 filled out accessory slots in bulk, including
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/Accessory_AirDash3/">Triple Air Dash Boots</a> (Lv 65),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/Accessory_JumpCount_Increase2/">Triple Jump Boots</a> (Lv 70) and
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/Accessory_AirDash2/">Double Air Dash Boots</a> (Lv 61)</li>
        <li><strong>Ancient Series armour</strong>: <a href="/en/tech-tree/AncientArmor/">Ancient Armor</a> (Lv 68),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/AncientHelmet/">Ancient Helm</a> (Lv 68) and
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/Shield_07/">Ancient Shield</a> (Lv 71) are the level 80 answer</li>
        <li><strong>Hexolite series</strong>: the Hexolite material line unlocked between Lv 58 and Lv 65, sitting between metal and ancient materials</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        All 588 tech points, each with its real unlock level from Lv 1 to Lv 80, are in the
        <a href="/en/tech-tree/">full tech tree</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Base and QoL Updates</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pal Effigy</strong> - the old "Lifmunk Effigy" was renamed to a generic name in 1.0</li>
        <li><strong>Wing Pack</strong> - a new decoration / utility item</li>
        <li><strong>Pal Expedition Station</strong> - expedition coverage now extends to Sunreach and the World Tree</li>
        <li><strong>Pal Labor Research Laboratory</strong> - a new research facility for base work Pals</li>
        <li><strong>Base Pal AI improvements</strong> (v1.0.4) - base automation behaves noticeably better</li>
        <li><strong>Predator Pals drop Predator Core</strong>, and the <strong>Negotiator</strong> Pal can cancel a <strong>Gold Coin Raid</strong></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>PvP and 15 New Dungeons</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>PvP</strong> - arena play arrived with 1.0, along with new PvP map regions</li>
        <li><strong>15 new dungeons in Feybreak</strong> - combined with the Ancient Relic Recycler and the Ancient Series techs, this closes the endgame material loop</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>72 New Pals, 287 in the Paldex</h2>
      <p>
        1.0 added <strong>72 Pals</strong> in one drop: <strong>47 new species</strong> plus
        <strong>25 variants</strong>, taking the Paldex to <strong>287</strong>. Most of them
        live in Sunreach and the World Tree, the two highest-level regions.
      </p>
      <p>
        To pick a core team, check the <a href="/en/tier-list/">Pal tier list</a>; for exact stats
        and drops, browse the <a href="/en/pals/">Pal database</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Patch History: 1.0 to v1.0.5</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>1.0 (2026-07-10)</strong> - patch 1.100.427, the 1.0 launch, out of Early Access</li>
        <li><strong>v1.0.4 (2026-09-07)</strong> - continuous Fisherman's Point side quests, improved base Pal AI, reworked fishing, PC frame-rate cap raised to 120 FPS</li>
        <li><strong>v1.0.5 (2026-09-15)</strong> - bug fixes only, the <strong>current latest version</strong>; there is no 1.1 yet</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        So a fresh save today is running 1.0 plus v1.0.5 - if you are following the fishing or
        side quest content, the v1.0.4 changes are the relevant ones.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="related-links">
      <h2>Related Guides</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/en/guides/boss-guide/">⚔️ All 9 tower boss strategies</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/regions/">🗺️ Palworld region index (80 regions)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/tech-tree/">🔬 Full tech tree (Lv 1-80)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/tier-list/">📊 Pal tier list</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/breeding/">🧮 Breeding calculator (mutant eggs)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/guides/beginner-guide/">🎮 Beginner guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/guides/base-building-guide/">🏠 Base building guide</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .guide-content { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.8; }
  .page-header { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .breadcrumb { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  h1 { font-size: 2rem; margin: 0.5rem 0; line-height: 1.3; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; color: var(--accent); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 0.8rem; }
  h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0.8rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  p { margin: 0.8rem 0; }
  ul, ol { margin: 0.8rem 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; }
  li { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
  a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }
  .related-links { margin-top: 3rem; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-secondary); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); }
  .related-links ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .related-links li { padding: 0.3rem 0; }
</style>
